<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Flag Maker: every text a player reads, in English. The source for every translation.

  To translate: copy this file, name it with the game's code for your language (de.xml, es.xml,
  fr.xml, ko.xml, pl.xml, pt.xml, ru.xml, zh.xml), set code and name below, and translate the
  text between the tags. Leave the keys alone.

  - {0}, {1}... are filled in by the mod (a number, a name). Keep every one of them.
  - A long text can be wrapped over several lines here: the break reads as one space.
  - \n is a real line break.
  - A key missing from a translation shows in English, so a partial translation works.

  Keep every text short: say it in as few words as get the message across.
  Tooltips: five words at most (they overflow otherwise). Say only what the label leaves out.
  Everyday words, American English.
-->
<Language code="en" name="English">

  <!-- ==================== The mod ==================== -->

  <!-- One line in the game's mods list: about 30 characters fit before it wraps. -->
  <String key="Mod.Description">Fully animated, customizable flags</String>
  <String key="Mod.Unsupported">
    Flag Maker can't draw flags on this computer: it needs Metal or OpenGL 3.3. Your flags stay
    saved in the city.
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.UnsupportedWindows">
    Flag Maker can't draw flags on this computer: it needs DirectX 11. Your flags stay saved in
    the city.\n\n
    Remove any graphics launch option (Steam: Properties, Launch Options) and restart.\n\n
    Still broken? Report it with the log:\n{0}
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.UnsupportedLinux">
    Flag Maker can't draw flags on this computer: it needs OpenGL 3.3. Your flags stay saved in
    the city.\n\n
    Or run the game's Windows version through Proton.\n\n
    Please report it with the log:\n{0}
  </String>

  <!-- A city whose flags this copy of the mod must leave alone: it stands down in the city, and
       the flags' saved designs are written back exactly as they were loaded. -->
  <String key="Mod.KeptUnreadable">
    Flag Maker can't read this city's flags (saved by a newer version, or damaged). It stays off
    here; saving keeps the flags as they are.\n\n
    Restart the game so Steam updates the mod.\n\n
    Still broken? Report it with the log:\n{0}
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.KeptEml">
    Flag Maker doesn't support Extended Managers Library yet (used by Prop Anarchy). It stays off
    here; saving keeps the flags as they are.
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.KeptLost">
    Flag Maker lost this city's {0} flag(s) while loading. Don't save: quit, restart the game and
    load again.\n\n
    Still missing? Report it with the log:\n{1}
  </String>

  <!-- Procedural Objects' or Move It's "Convert to PO" on a flag: refused, the flag left as it is. -->
  <String key="Mod.NoProcedural">Flags can't become Procedural Objects. They stay as they are.</String>

  <!-- Shown once ever: the first time new flags in a crowd were switched to Loop. -->
  <String key="Mod.CrowdLoop">
    Many waving flags close together slow the game down, so new flags here are placed as Loop:
    it looks much the same and costs almost nothing.\n\n
    Want them waving? Choose Waving in the New flag window, or turn off Place crowds as Loop in
    Settings.
  </String>

